      "flags": {},
      "order": 2,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Muse Fish 2 Voice Clone\n\n**Built with Fish Audio.** Fish Audio S2 Pro is **non-commercial only**. For commercial use, ask business@fish.audio.\n\n## 1. Node packs you need\nUse **ComfyUI Manager → Install Missing Custom Nodes**, then restart ComfyUI.\n\n- **Fish S2 Pro nodes** (they do the speaking, so you need these): [ComfyUI-FishAudioS2](https://github.com/Saganaki22/ComfyUI-FishAudioS2)\n- **Muse nodes** (the Prompter and Whisper): [Muse-Fish-S2-Pro-Voice-Clone](https://github.com/muse-collective-26/Muse-Fish-S2-Pro-Voice-Clone)\n- **FL Audio Separation**: [ComfyUI_Fill-Nodes](https://github.com/filliptm/ComfyUI_Fill-Nodes)\n- **Load Audio (Upload)**: [ComfyUI-VideoHelperSuite](https://github.com/Kosinkadink/ComfyUI-VideoHelperSuite)\n\n## 2. Models (they download by themselves on the first run)\n- **Fish S2 Pro.** Pick one in **model_path** on the Fish node. Files go in `ComfyUI/models/fishaudioS2/`.\n  - `s2-pro-fp8`: [drbaph/s2-pro-fp8](https://huggingface.co/drbaph/s2-pro-fp8). About 12 GB VRAM, and needs an RTX 4090 or 5090.\n  - `s2-pro`: [fishaudio/s2-pro](https://huggingface.co/fishaudio/s2-pro). Full size, about 24 GB VRAM.\n  - `s2-pro-bnb-int8` (about 8–9 GB) or `s2-pro-bnb-nf4` (about 4–5 GB): for smaller GPUs. These need `bitsandbytes` installed.\n- **Whisper large-v3**: [openai/whisper-large-v3](https://huggingface.co/openai/whisper-large-v3). About 3 GB.\n- **HDemucs**: the vocal split model. It's small.\n\n## 3. How to use\n1. **Reference Voice:** upload 5–15 seconds of clear speech. Only use a voice you have permission to use.\n2. **Dialogue You Want Spoken:** type your script.\n3. **Prompter:** pick a provider, press **↻ Models**, then choose a model.\n   - Ollama and LM Studio are free and run on your computer.\n   - ChatGPT needs `OPENAI_API_KEY` set in the environment, and Gemini needs `GEMINI_API_KEY`.\n4. Press **Run**. The audio is saved in `output/Muse/Audio/`.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# Muse Fish 2 Voice Clone\n\n**Built with Fish Audio.** Fish Audio S2 Pro is **non-commercial only**. For commercial use, ask business@fish.audio.\n\n## 1. Node packs you need\nUse **ComfyUI Manager → Install Missing Custom Nodes**, then restart ComfyUI.\n\n- **Fish S2 Pro nodes** (they do the speaking, so you need these): [ComfyUI-FishAudioS2](https://github.com/Saganaki22/ComfyUI-FishAudioS2)\n- **Muse nodes** (the Prompter and Whisper): [Muse-Fish-S2-Pro-Voice-Clone](https://github.com/muse-collective-26/Muse-Fish-S2-Pro-Voice-Clone)\n- **FL Audio Separation**: [ComfyUI_Fill-Nodes](https://github.com/filliptm/ComfyUI_Fill-Nodes)\n- **Load Audio (Upload)**: [ComfyUI-VideoHelperSuite](https://github.com/Kosinkadink/ComfyUI-VideoHelperSuite)\n\n## 2. Models (they download by themselves on the first run)\n- **Fish S2 Pro.** Pick one in **model_path** on the Fish node. Files go in `ComfyUI/models/fishaudioS2/`.\n  - `s2-pro-fp8`: [drbaph/s2-pro-fp8](https://huggingface.co/drbaph/s2-pro-fp8). About 12 GB VRAM, and needs an RTX 4090 or 5090.\n  - `s2-pro`: [fishaudio/s2-pro](https://huggingface.co/fishaudio/s2-pro). Full size, about 24 GB VRAM.\n  - `s2-pro-bnb-int8` (about 8–9 GB) or `s2-pro-bnb-nf4` (about 4–5 GB): for smaller GPUs. These need `bitsandbytes` installed.\n- **Whisper large-v3**: [openai/whisper-large-v3](https://huggingface.co/openai/whisper-large-v3). About 3 GB.\n- **HDemucs**: the vocal split model. It's small.\n\n## 3. How to use\n1. **Reference Voice:** upload 5–15 seconds of clear speech. Only use a voice you have permission to use.\n2. **Dialogue You Want Spoken:** type your script.\n3. **Prompter:** pick a provider, press **↻ Models**, then choose a model.\n   - Ollama and LM Studio are free and run on your computer.\n   - ChatGPT needs `OPENAI_API_KEY` set in the environment, and Gemini needs `GEMINI_API_KEY`.\n4. Press **Run**. The audio is saved in `output/Muse/Audio/`.\n"
      },
      "color": "#cf2a2a",
      "bgcolor": "#3e2525",
      "title": "Read me: node packs + models"
    }
